f Mennaeus was the ruler of the Ituraeans in the 1st century BCE, with his capital at Chalcis in the Beqaa valley.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-vi-philometor"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ptolemy-vi-philometor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ptolemy VI Philometor</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ptolemy VI Philometor was king of Ptolemaic Egypt from 180 to 145 BCE, at times jointly with his brother Ptolemy VIII and his sister-wife Cleopatra II.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-viii-physcon"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ptolemy-viii-physcon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ptolemy VIII Physcon</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ptolemy VIII, nicknamed Physcon, was a Ptolemaic king who quarrelled for decades with his brother Ptolemy VI.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-xii-auletes"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ptolemy-xii-auletes.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ptolemy XII Auletes</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ptolemy XII Auletes was king of Ptolemaic Egypt from 80 to 58 BCE and again from 55 to 51 BCE, and father of Cleopatra VII.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pua-district"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pua-district.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pua district</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Pua is a district in the upper Nan valley of Nan Province in northern Thailand.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/puabi"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/puabi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Puabi</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Puabi was a queen or noblewoman of Ur around 2600 BCE, known from her richly furnished tomb in the Royal Cemetery, excavated by Leonard Woolley in 1927–1928.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/publius-canidius-crassus"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/publius-canidius-crassus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Publius Canidius Crassus</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Publius Canidius Crassus was a Roman general and partisan of Mark Antony, suffect consul in 40 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/publius-carisius"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/publius-carisius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Publius Carisius</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Publius Carisius was a Roman general under Augustus, legate in Hispania Ulterior during the Cantabrian Wars.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/publius-cornelius-scipio-consul-218-bce"><span class="enc-name">Publius Cornelius Scipio (consul 218 BCE)</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Publius Cornelius Scipio was a Roman consul of 218 BCE and the father of Scipio Africanus.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/publius-cornelius-scipio-nasica-consul-191-bc"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/publius-cornelius-scipio-nasica-consul-191-bc.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Publius Cornelius Scipio Nasica (consul 191 BC)</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Publius Cornelius Scipio Nasica was a Roman politician, the son of Gnaeus Scipio Calvus.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/publius-cornelius-scipio-nasica-corculum"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/publius-cornelius-scipio-nasica-corculum.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Publius Cornelius Scipio Nasica Corculum</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Publius Cornelius Scipio Nasica Corculum was a Roman statesman and general, consul in 162 and 155 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/publius-licinius-crassus"><span class="enc-name">Publius Licinius Crassus</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Publius Licinius Crassus was a son of the triumvir Marcus Crassus and a legate of Julius Caesar in the Gallic Wars.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/publius-ostorius-scapula"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/publius-ostorius-scapula.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Publius Ostorius Scapula</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Publius Ostorius Scapula was Roman governor of Britain from 47 to 52.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/publius-quinctilius-varus"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/publius-quinctilius-varus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Publius Quinctilius Varus</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Publius Quinctilius Varus was a Roman general and governor.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/publius-servilius-vatia-isauricus"><span class="enc-name">Publius Servilius Vatia Isauricus</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Publius Servilius Vatia Isauricus was a Roman general and statesman, consul in 79 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/publius-sittius"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/enc