-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/puduhepa"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/puduhepa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Puduhepa</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Puduhepa was a Hittite queen of the 13th century BCE, wife of Hattusili III and the daughter of a priest of Lawazantiya in Kizzuwatna.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/puebla-state"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/puebla-state.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Puebla (state)</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Puebla is a state of central Mexico, east of Mexico City, with its capital at the city of Puebla.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/puebla-tlaxcala-valley"><span class="enc-name">Puebla-Tlaxcala Valley</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Puebla-Tlaxcala Valley is a highland basin of central Mexico, east of the volcanoes Popocatépetl and Iztaccíhuatl, shared by the modern states of Puebla and Tlaxcala.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pueblo-bonito"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pueblo-bonito.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pueblo Bonito</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Pueblo Bonito is the largest great house of Chaco Canyon in northern New Mexico, built in stages by the Ancestral Puebloans and occupied between 828 and 1126.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pueblo-peoples"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pueblo-peoples.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pueblo peoples</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Pueblo peoples are Native American communities of the south-